>>__ load "splitLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SPLIT_TAC`

``` hol4
splitLib.SPLIT_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Performs one case split with split rules.

A split rule is a theorem without hypotheses of the form

``` hol4
|- !P ... . P (c a1 ... an) = rhs
```

where `P` is a Boolean-valued variable and `c` a constant. It is an
assumption rule if `rhs` is a negation, and a conclusion rule otherwise.
`splitLib.type_split_rules ty` gives both rules for the case constant of
datatype `ty`; `splitLib.type_split_of ty` gives the conclusion rule.

`SPLIT_TAC rules` rewrites the conclusion with one instance of a
conclusion rule: the matching redex under the fewest binders it depends
on, outermost and leftmost first, with `P` taken as the enclosing
formula. If no conclusion rule applies, it rewrites the first assumption
to which an assumption rule applies and strips the result, producing a
goal per case.

### Failure

Fails if a rule is malformed, or if no rule applies.

### Example

``` hol4
>>__ val c = Context.snapshot();
>> splitLib.SPLIT_TAC [splitLib.type_split_of “:bool”]
     ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) c;
>> splitLib.SPLIT_TAC (splitLib.type_split_rules “:bool”)
     ([“P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”], “Q : bool”) c;
```

### Comments

To split on a chosen term throughout a goal, use `Cases_on` or
`CASE_TAC`.

